WEBVTT

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.230
Any girl that goes to Altair either dies or transforms into a man.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.670
Does that mean Mix...?

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.470
We found her, but she wasn't Mix anymore.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.200
She'd lost her memories.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.360
Are Zessica and Yunoha all right?

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.010
We're all right now.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.120
The checkups didn't find anything wrong.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.270
But if we'd been there just a little longer...

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.410
Did Mikono come back yet?

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.020
No, she's still searching for High Commander Fudo.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.640
How's Shrade?

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.900
The worst of it has passed, but he needs to rest for a while.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.460
So the High Commander is missing, and Shrade's down and out?

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.100
Neo-Deava is good as dead!

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.980
Don't give up so easily!

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.800
It's not over yet.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.290
We should regroup and head back up to Altair!

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.730
Andy?

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.580
I will save Mix.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.970
Andy...

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:13.910
Are you okay?

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:15.480
I'm fine!

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:23.520
I'm not giving up. I'll get Mix back if it's the last thing I do!

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:02.280
I was so close. I almost saw it.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:08.130
The perfect melody of love echoing between two worlds.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.540
Don't talk.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.750
You have to rest.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:22.700
Will I finish composing it before my life runs out?

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:28.760
Can you tell me with your Prophecy of Despair?

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.770
You really want to hear your dark future?

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:39.530
Sorrow makes some songs all the more beautiful.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.340
Shrade...

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:49.810
If I finish the song, will you play it with me, my friend?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.300
When will High Commander Fudo return?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.680
We haven't heard anything from Mikono, either.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.630
Please have one, Miss Suomi.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.390
No, thank you. I try to avoid eating high calorie foods late at night.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.380
I see.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.430
Please don't worry.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.540
Fudo will return to us.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.630
And he'll bring back the legend of Genesis.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.610
Girl with hair the color of grass.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:32.290
Such a shame. I even opened the gate for you...

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.540
You!

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.950
Don't forget to keep your promise.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:48.010
What promise? I didn't promise you anything...

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:51.970
Even if you don't remember what it was,

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.520
you will keep it for me when the time comes.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.120
Mix...

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.590
I actually saw her big bangs.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:26.010
But they weren't big bangs at all.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.500
Andy, what are you doing here?

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.390
If I don't sit right here, I'll sink.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.600
That's one of the holes Mix filled.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:44.960
Yep. There are absolutely no weak points in the material she fills with.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.030
I can't sink into it even if my power overloads.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:53.920
Andy...

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.300
Amata...

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.770
Say we actually got Mix back.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:01.340
Would I...

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.950
I mean, now that she's a boy,

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:08.130
would I still love her the same?

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:28.110
Well, well. I didn't smell anyone, but here you are.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.040
Let go of me!

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.380
Why are you running away?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.430
We're finally one!

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:45.960
Apollo...

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.540
Here I am, Apollo.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.060
I've been waiting to see you again.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:56.970
You came for me!

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:58.600
Mikono...

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.460
Wrong, wench.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.730
We're not Apollon.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.940
We're Amagura!

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.990
Mikono, wait!

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.660
Hold it right there, wench!

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.110
Let go of her!

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:20.710
Shut up!

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.790
Join us, wench.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.410
Help!

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.470
Amata, stop!

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.980
Mikono...

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.780
Thank you.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:09.380
What remains between your hands when you clap them?

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.820
A right hand and a left. Angel and human.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:17.300
Man and woman. Plus and minus.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.890
What is in the gap between them?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.230
What's in the gap between my right hand and my left?

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.160
Nothing.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.650
There's nothing there, but it feels warm.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.980
Haven't I heard this somewhere before?

00:08:56.610 --> 00:09:01.970
Long ago, just after the heavens and earth were separated,

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:05.310
the world was bathed in a glorious light.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:11.980
The flowers sang, while the creatures and insects whispered of love.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:15.850
The angels made love among the stars.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:22.610
But the angels were hunters, and mankind was their prey.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:30.130
In this war, there fought an Angel of Slaughter named Apollonius,

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:35.470
but he met a girl named Celiane, and they fell in love.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:42.520
Apollonius betrayed his kind and allied with the humans.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:52.260
The traitor cast off his wings and gave unto the humans a great weapon.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.860
He piloted a machine Angel and fought against the angels.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.490
This is the legend written in the Book of Genesis.

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:05.200
And is that what really happened 12,000 years ago?

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.290
No.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:12.800
This is the previous story, the story of 24,000 years ago.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:20.780
The wheel of Fate has turned again, and the legend is about to be told once more.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.080
Once more...

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.810
Amata Sora! Explain yourself!

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:39.720
I do not recall ordering a sortie!

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.570
I'm going after Mikono.

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:44.240
You were not given permission to move out!

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.220
She's calling me.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.000
Mikono is calling for help.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.210
I have to get to her quickly!

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.450
Mikono...

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:05.720
I can't let someone I love leave me again...

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:14.460
Yes, go to the one you love,

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.650
and to the Wings of the Sun.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:24.160
And you, fragmented one, wake up now.

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:32.250
Amata...

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:36.420
Vector Z's transmitter is turned off. We can't track it.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:41.250
Cayenne, can you see where it is with the Prophecy of Despair?

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.540
I'll try.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.320
No...

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:13.050
This is the city where Mikono and I first met.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:19.440
What happened here?

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:51.250
Where is this?

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:56.760
The gap between light and darkness, as written in the Book of Genesis.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.240
The cockpit's empty.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.650
Where did Amata go?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.860
The city where Amata and I first met.

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:11.940
And where we had our first Union.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.980
No one's here.

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:26.610
Where did they all go?

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:33.000
I'd heard it was locked down after that fight,

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.590
but I didn't know it was this bad.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:38.110
Is Mikono here, too?

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:40.380
According to my power.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:45.480
So you did come after Mikono, Amata...

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:48.110
Let's split up and search.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:13:59.810
Sir?

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:29.680
What are these?

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.930
They aren't mine. Whose are they?

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:38.140
What am I supposed to do?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:42.350
Why did Mikage send me here?

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.020
It smells...

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:52.520
I'm sure I was here, a long time ago.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:20.970
Amata...

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:44.920
You've finally unlocked those suppressed memories.

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:52.210
"Skies of Aquaria"?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.840
Mikono...

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.830
Mikono!

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.210
Amata!

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:31.190
Zessica? What are you doing here?

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:35.250
I came to get you, Amata.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.570
I mean, Chairman Crea ordered us.

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:42.350
Me and Cayenne.

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:47.110
Sorry. It's my fault for going against orders.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:57.040
This whole town is locked down, so everyone was evacuated.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:00.740
So that's why there's no one left.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.540
Why did you have to come here so badly? You even disobeyed orders.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.950
I don't know, but...

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.130
But what?

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:13.010
I felt like Mikono was calling for me.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:20.350
I'll be waiting for you.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:25.020
Even if I have to wait for 12,000 years.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:34.320
You used to work in this theater, right, Amata?

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:38.360
And this is where you met Mikono?

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.280
Zessica?

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:44.540
Amata... Next time...

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:48.870
After the next 12,000 years...

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.120
I...

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:03.680
It is not the place of you humans to write your own false tales.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:08.980
Not when a true legend is about to come to pass again!

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:13.860
Zessica!

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.570
Run! This way!

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:19.360
What's the matter? Come on!

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:32.960
Run, little beasts of love, run.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.870
Run to the promised land!

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:50.810
Amata!

00:18:54.760 --> 00:19:00.730
Zessica!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.200
Ugh!

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:07.680
Stop. I'm not getting out.

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:09.210
You don't know that!

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.650
Forget about me! Just go!

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:20.180
Never! I won't leave you behind!

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:22.620
Amata...

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.100
Thank you, Amata.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.910
Zessica! No!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.000
Zessica!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.570
We've been looking for you, Amata!

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:21.800
We're here, Cayenne!

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.280
Sazanka!

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.160
Vector Y! Who's in it?

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:31.160
You said that when I finished the piece, you would play it with me, my friend.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:34.920
Cut it out! You can't Unite in your condition!

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:40.420
There's no time for that! Come!

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.640
Life-on-the-line Union!

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.970
Go, Aquarion!

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:52.560
Shrade, why...

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.770
Thank you, my friend.

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:57.770
This is so rotten!

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:02.660
Aquarion Spada!

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:21.000
Found you, Amata, you pathetic wimp.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:23.760
You are...

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:35.890
The Wings of the Sun will soon awaken.

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:38.850
I have to say I'm sorry...

00:21:40.530 --> 00:21:44.380
Please, forgive me... for what I did to you...

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:50.630
You... You saw it.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:53.910
Yeah. I didn't think it was real.

00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:17.470
And I saw Amata, pathetically unable to do a thing about it.

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:26.030
So you're...

00:22:26.970 --> 00:22:28.050
Yeah.

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:32.280
You're me.

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:18.060
I think that Kagura might be a little wrong about girls.

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:22.200
Loving someone is supposed to be more kind and gentle.

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:24.560
Oh, no!
